# GitHub's Linguist picks the project language by counting code lines.
# A Flutter project auto-generates native "platform" scaffolding
# (windows/, linux/, ios/, macos/, android/) full of C/C++/Swift code.
# That generated code is often bigger than the actual Dart codebase, so
# GitHub mis-labels such repos as C++/Kotlin/etc.

# 1) Treat generated native platform folders as vendored code: they are
#    excluded from GitHub's language statistics entirely.
windows/** linguist-vendored
linux/** linguist-vendored
macos/** linguist-vendored
ios/** linguist-vendored
android/** linguist-vendored

# 2) Explicitly label the real source of our app as Dart.
*.dart linguist-language=Dart
